root[203]
├─0   heading[1]
│     │ depth: 1
│     └─0 text "Contributing to Ruff"
├─1   paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "Welcome! We're happy to have you here. Thank you in advance for your contribution to Ruff."
├─2   blockquote[2]
│     ├─0 paragraph[1]
│     │   └─0 text "[!NOTE]"
│     └─1 paragraph[3]
│         ├─0 text "This guide is for Ruff. If you're looking to contribute to ty, please see "
│         ├─1 link[1]
│         │   │ title: null
│         │   │ url: "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/crates/ty/CONTRIBUTING.md"
│         │   └─0 text "the ty contributing\nguide"
│         └─2 text "."
├─3   heading[1]
│     │ depth: 2
│     └─0 text "Finding ways to help"
├─4   paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "We label issues that would be good for a first time contributor as\n"
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22"
│     │   └─0 inlineCode "good first issue"
│     └─2 text ".\nThese usually do not require significant experience with Rust or the Ruff code base."
├─5   paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "We label issues that we think are a good opportunity for subsequent contributions as\n"
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22help+wanted%22"
│     │   └─0 inlineCode "help wanted"
│     └─2 text ".\nThese require varying levels of experience with Rust and Ruff. Often, we want to accomplish these\ntasks but do not have the resources to do so ourselves."
├─6   paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "You don't need our permission to start on an issue we have labeled as appropriate for community\ncontribution as described above. However, it's a good idea to indicate that you are going to work on\nan issue to avoid concurrent attempts to solve the same problem."
├─7   paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "Please check in with us before starting work on an issue that has not been labeled as appropriate\nfor community contribution. We're happy to receive contributions for other issues, but it's\nimportant to make sure we have consensus on the solution to the problem first."
├─8   paragraph[9]
│     ├─0 text "Outside of issues with the labels above, issues labeled as\n"
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22bug%22"
│     │   └─0 inlineCode "bug"
│     ├─2 text " are the\nbest candidates for contribution. In contrast, issues labeled with "
│     ├─3 inlineCode "needs-decision"
│     ├─4 text " or\n"
│     ├─5 inlineCode "needs-design"
│     ├─6 text " are "
│     ├─7 emphasis[1]
│     │   └─0 text "not"
│     └─8 text " good candidates for contribution. Please do not open pull requests for\nissues with these labels."
├─9   paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "Please do not open pull requests for new features without prior discussion. While we appreciate\nexploration of new features, we will often close these pull requests immediately. Adding a\nnew feature to ruff creates a long-term maintenance burden and requires strong consensus from the ruff\nteam before it is appropriate to begin work on an implementation."
├─10  heading[1]
│     │ depth: 3
│     └─0 text "Avoiding duplicate work"
├─11  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "Before starting on an issue, take a look at the discussion and any linked pull requests, including\nthose in the sidebar. An issue may still be open while a fix is under review. Even if a previous\nattempt was closed, it may contain useful context or review comments that you could incorporate\nbefore submitting a new PR."
├─12  heading[1]
│     │ depth: 2
│     └─0 text "Use of AI"
├─13  paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "We "
│     ├─1 strong[2]
│     │   ├─0 text "require all use of AI in contributions to follow our\n"
│     │   └─1 link[1]
│     │       │ title: null
│     │       │ url: "https://github.com/astral-sh/.github/blob/main/AI_POLICY.md"
│     │       └─0 text "AI Policy"
│     └─2 text "."
├─14  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "If your contribution does not follow the policy, it will be closed."
├─15  heading[1]
│     │ depth: 3
│     └─0 text "Local skills for Codex or Claude"
├─16  paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "This repository includes local agent skills for ty development under "
│     ├─1 inlineCode ".agents/skills"
│     └─2 text "."
├─17  paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "Contributors using Codex for development should find that Codex auto-discovers the skills and uses\nthem automatically when necessary. Claude Code users may be prompted to install the\n"
│     ├─1 inlineCode "ty-skills@ruff-agent-skills"
│     └─2 text " local plugin. If the skills are not installed automatically, install\nthem manually from the repository root by running these slash commands inside Claude Code:"
├─18  code "/plugin marketplace add ./.agents\n/plugin install ty-skills@ruff-agent-skills"
│       lang: "text"
│       meta: null
