│     └─0 text "Development"
├─29  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "After cloning the repository, run Ruff locally from the repository root with:"
├─30  code "cargo run -p ruff -- check /path/to/file.py --no-cache"
│       lang: "shell"
│       meta: null
├─31  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "Prior to opening a pull request, ensure that your code has been auto-formatted,\nand that it passes both the lint and test validation checks:"
├─32  code "cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings  # Rust linting\nRUFF_UPDATE_SCHEMA=1 cargo test  # Rust testing and updating ruff.schema.json\nuv run --only-dev --locked prek run --all-files  # Rust and Python formatting, Markdown and Python linting, etc."
│       lang: "shell"
│       meta: null
├─33  paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "These checks will run on GitHub Actions when you open your pull request, but running them locally\nwill save you time and expedite the merge process."
