│     │       │    └─0 text "Same-package"
│     │       ├─1  text ": the imported module is in the same package as the current file. This gets back\nto the importance of the \"package root\" and the file's \"module path\". Imagine that we're\nanalyzing "
│     │       ├─2  inlineCode "baz.py"
│     │       ├─3  text " above. If "
│     │       ├─4  inlineCode "baz.py"
│     │       ├─5  text " contains any imports that appear to come from the "
